g the CBS Television programs Suspense, Studio One Summer Theatre, Climax!, The Best of Broadway and Playhouse 90. He was the sole producer of the award-winning drama series, Playhouse 90, during its first two seasons from 1956 to 1958.\nAfter leaving Playhouse 90, Manulis was the \"head of television\" for 20th Century Fox Television where he was responsible for creating and producing the series, The Many Loves of Dobie Gillis, Adventures in Paradise, and Five Fingers.  In 1962, he produced the film Days of Wine and Roses starring Jack Lemmon and Lee Remick.", "biography_author": "Wikidata", "date_of_biography": "2022-05-19T12:24:22.304540+10:00", "external_links": [{"id": 2660, "uri": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Martin_Manulis"}], "uuid": "5a20e9d5-22c1-4c75-9872-d5f4391421ec", "source": {"name": "Vernon", "slug": "vernon"}, "source_identifier": "24650", "external_references": [{"id": 11357, "source": {"name": "Wikidata", "slug": "wikidata"}, "source_identifier": "Q1904542"}, {"id": 11358, "source": {"name": "VIAF", "slug": "viaf"}, "source_identifier": "34016110"}, {"id": 11359, "source": {"name": "LOC Auth", "slug": "loc-auth"}, "source_identifier": "no90014904"}, {"id": 11360, "source": {"name": "WorldCat", "slug": "worldcat"}, "source_identifier": "lccn-no90014904"}], "date_modified": "2023-09-13T12:31:16.645166+10:00"}, {"id": 24407, "name": "Embassy Pictures Corporation (US)", "roles_in_work": [{"id": 1987140, "title": "The Graduate", "work_id": 83178, "role": "production company", "role_id": 941, "is_primary": true}, {"id": 2649896, "title": "Long day's journey into night", "work_id": 82358, "role": "production company", "role_id": 941, "is_primary": true}, {"id": 813848, "title": "The Graduate (Special edition)", "work_id": 93020, "role": "production company", "role_id": 941, "is_primary": true}, {"id": 2476488, "title": "Into the straight", "work_id": 87693, "role": "production company", "role_id": 941, "is_primary": true}, {"id": 2177273, "title": "Da